 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "O'er the new moon's golden beam,\nI've read \"The Dandy,\" essay\nBy a young Marquis of burgundy\nWho, with the truth and poetry way,\nMade his name in Paris.\nHe set out on celebration\nOf a world-renown friend whose glory\nWas novel for his country nation;\nAnd in love of it admired,\nHis father-sense had reputation.\nBut not so much was he for beauty,\nAs only for his sadness. Everyone",
